#
# Oracle 8.1.7's reply to OCI 9.2's BEGIN :r := 'got ' || :g; END; with
# 'a value' for :g (#2804): the bind prompt (OUT, IN), the OUT value, the status.
# Captured 2026-11-26 through tcpdump on the 9i VM. The TTC payload,
# without the packet's header, as `hexdump -C` output; the offset column
# and the |ascii| gutter are ignored by tests.replay.parse_hexdump.
00000000  0b 05 02 00 00 00 01 00  00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  |................|
00000010  00 00 10 20 07 0b 67 6f  74 20 61 20 76 61 6c 75  |... ..got a valu|
00000020  65 00 00 08 04 00 b4 f9  36 00 00 00 00 00 01 00  |e.......6.......|
00000030  00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  00 00 04 01 00 00 00 00  |................|
00000040  00 00 00 00 00 01 00 00  00 2f 00 40 00 00 00 00  |........./.@....|
00000050  00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  |................|
00000060  00 05 00 00 01 00 00 00  00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  |................|
00000070  00 00 00 00 00 00                                 |......|
00000076
